s:56481:"{
"lastpushid": 320,
"pushes": {"100": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D130972", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/onecrl.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "19038e883edec2dd54276016fafc9212156f1ca6", "parents": ["64367abc670d7c625e630272871a7e2d6073a6cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1739040 - Upgrade cc to v1.0.71. r=emilio, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D130227", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/cc/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/cc/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/cc/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/cc/README.md", "third_party/rust/cc/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/cc/src/windows_registry.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "09f147960f62b26cf61a45c24d7e29e79b7f990c", "parents": ["19038e883edec2dd54276016fafc9212156f1ca6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1739040 - Pick cc upstream patch for GCC 11 on armhf linux. r=emilio, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D130228", "files": [".cargo/config.in", "Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/cc/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/cc/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/cc/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/cc/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ee97a378a4361db4fab1472b1995bcf30faab091", "parents": ["09f147960f62b26cf61a45c24d7e29e79b7f990c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kirk Steuber \u003cksteuber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1728536 - Fix --disable-maintenance-service build capability. r=nalexander, a=RyanVM\n\nBuilding without support for the maintenance service currently does not work because the definitions of EnvHasValue and IsSecureUpdateStatusSucceeded are ifdef'ed out despite being used. This patch fixes this by including those functions, even if compiling without support for the maintenance service.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D129722", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dd5cd481c039241d0738246fc8303283ff954be4", "parents": ["ee97a378a4361db4fab1472b1995bcf30faab091"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alwu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722171 - use time threshold to determine if we need to skip to next key frame. r=bryce, a=RyanVM\n\nIn bug1692881, we introduced a mechanism to skip to next key frame if video decoding is too slow, which aims to help slow decoding issue on high resolution videos. Eg. 4k+.\n\nHowever, there are some cases which would also lead to slow decoding. Eg. when internal seek (seek on one track only) happens on a place where we can't seek to directly, we need to seek to the previous keyframe and then decode all of them until we get the target frame.\n\nThat could lead to spending huge amount of time if the target frame is far from the keyframe, and causes decoded video frame later than the media time because audio won't stop playing during video seek. However, in above example, there would only be few frames later than the media time, and the video will soon catch up with the time.\n\nAs we only want to trigger this mechanism for continually slow decoding problem, and completely removing this mechanism would lead us fallback to the situation where some 4K+ videos would be frozen all the time during the playback.\n\nIn this patch, we introduce a method which still keep this mechanism but won't perform that as aggressive as before, this uses the time threshold to seek to the next keyframe when video has been late for too long.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D126858", "files": ["dom/media/MediaDecoderStateMachine.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "12c7011b33abcce19753616dd7c1ed3a20914001", "parents": ["dd5cd481c039241d0738246fc8303283ff954be4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1717553 - Take WeakMap mark color into account when marking delegates. r=sfink, a=RyanVM\n\nI'm not sure why this was changed, although I expect it's something we\ndiscussed at the time.\n\nI changed the two places that definitely need it but I'm not sure whether\nmarkEntries needs to change too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D127547", "files": ["js/src/gc/WeakMap-inl.h", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/weak-marking-03.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "aa9b5e2a7c66825fc1a80a1bc8748f9f0e549d7e", "parents": ["12c7011b33abcce19753616dd7c1ed3a20914001"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Zuehlcke \u003cpbz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1720926 - Rate limit calls to location.reload. r=smaug, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D128636", "files": ["docshell/test/navigation/test_rate_limit_location_change.html", "dom/base/Location.cpp", "dom/base/Location.h", "dom/base/nsHistory.cpp", "dom/base/nsHistory.h", "dom/webidl/History.webidl"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ffde89696567ff6de38a9ee45a2bed79d7c3aebc", "parents": ["aa9b5e2a7c66825fc1a80a1bc8748f9f0e549d7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Zuehlcke \u003cpbz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1696685 - r=valentin,nika a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D128630", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsINetUtil.idl", "uriloader/exthandler/nsExternalHelperAppService.cpp", "uriloader/exthandler/nsExternalHelperAppService.h", "xpcom/io/nsEscape.cpp", "xpcom/io/nsEscape.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "800cc8dc7639112299e51d7b710fb434731c7edf", "parents": ["ffde89696567ff6de38a9ee45a2bed79d7c3aebc"], "tags": []}], "date": 1636641741, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "101": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1728536 - Fix macOS build bustage. r=bytesized, a=bustage", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "882637f560a406777419b659d1651f2972f50bf1", "parents": ["800cc8dc7639112299e51d7b710fb434731c7edf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1717318: Test-case for bug. r=mjf, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D124061", "files": ["dom/media/tests/crashtests/1717318.html", "dom/media/tests/crashtests/crashtests.list"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2c9565d45c472a932fe812f056130f560feb4f07", "parents": ["882637f560a406777419b659d1651f2972f50bf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1717318: Stop PeerConnectionImpl from crashing if constructed with a null global. r=mjf, a=RyanVM\n\nDepends on D124061\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D124062", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCStatsReport.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4b0d941ab1a32ee34cd62086aca5102a154cf1a4", "parents": ["2c9565d45c472a932fe812f056130f560feb4f07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1728574 - make sure Performance pointer is valid before using. r=ng, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D125442", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCStatsReport.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c81e8fbec9f3c3821dc292c2925a22694dc589d2", "parents": ["4b0d941ab1a32ee34cd62086aca5102a154cf1a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1737751 - Account for macOS cursor scaling. r=emilio, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D129521", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "widget/LookAndFeel.h", "widget/cocoa/nsLookAndFeel.mm", "widget/nsXPLookAndFeel.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ba9ee45df167602f2b8a8ffddc53ac1220d38d87", "parents": ["c81e8fbec9f3c3821dc292c2925a22694dc589d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1393362 - Make more RecordedEvent implementations fallible. r=bobowen a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D129879", "files": ["gfx/2d/RecordedEvent.h", "gfx/2d/RecordedEventImpl.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7683a726aed33c76494db546f157182a138a58b3", "parents": ["ba9ee45df167602f2b8a8ffddc53ac1220d38d87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1736751 - Use swap in ThreadEventQueue::SetObserver. r=KrisWright, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D129031", "files": ["xpcom/threads/ThreadEventQueue.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ee62e4f1b5f0fddf93939de8e8ddc829fa17e33d", "parents": ["7683a726aed33c76494db546f157182a138a58b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1737009 - Make `nsTextFragment::SetTo()` check given string length first r=smaug, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D129137", "files": ["dom/base/nsTextFragment.cpp", "dom/base/nsTextFragment.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "803f6a4707ed4435d4284552b4c808134975563b", "parents": ["ee62e4f1b5f0fddf93939de8e8ddc829fa17e33d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1636653431, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "102": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset 803f6a4707ed (bug 1737009) for bustage.", "files": ["dom/base/nsTextFragment.cpp", "dom/base/nsTextFragment.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7f2dd2d469a616664b4fb7c913955b956ed2b42e", "parents": ["803f6a4707ed4435d4284552b4c808134975563b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1737009 - Make `nsTextFragment::SetTo()` check given string length first. r=smaug, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D129148", "files": ["dom/base/nsTextFragment.cpp", "dom/base/nsTextFragment.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "bd4d7d89779a2299d2b0e00049d951956f5a8735", "parents": ["7f2dd2d469a616664b4fb7c913955b956ed2b42e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1636654553, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "103": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D131119", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/main/password-recipes.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "90e6faeb97dad97582a6de888ccb525db09199f8", "parents": ["bd4d7d89779a2299d2b0e00049d951956f5a8735"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1738237, don't try to create too large string buffers, r=mccr8, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D130041", "files": ["dom/base/nsStructuredCloneContainer.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "da53bf5bac5da0dbc69fa6ec8c01afeaf187829a", "parents": ["90e6faeb97dad97582a6de888ccb525db09199f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Geoff Lankow \u003cgeoff@darktrojan.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740381 - Port bug 1736565 (Infer artifact build candidate tree based on version) for comm- trees. r=nalexander a=RyanVM\n\nThis is the same configuration as for mozilla- trees as added in https://hg.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/rev/93e421a84361 except Thunderbird doesn't use comm-release.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D130817", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifacts.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_artifacts.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "918cd8f5c2e9ac67cf2687dfe9842c86a03cf175", "parents": ["da53bf5bac5da0dbc69fa6ec8c01afeaf187829a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1716883 - fix autoscroll behaviour over various SVG elements, r=masayuki a=RyanVM\n\nThis avoids starting autoscroll on SVG links, and on HTML links that\ncontain SVG, by sharing the code that browser's ClickHandlerChild uses\nto detect links into BrowserUtils, and using that from AutoScrollChild\nto determine if the click happened on top of a link. It also adds a\ntest so we avoid regressing this in future.\n\nWhen running the test, I noticed an error from ClickHandlerParent\nwhen the browser for which we receive a click has gone away, and\nfixed it by adding a nullcheck and early return.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120024", "files": ["browser/actors/ClickHandlerChild.jsm", "browser/actors/ClickHandlerParent.jsm", "toolkit/actors/AutoScrollChild.jsm", "toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser.ini", "toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_autoscroll_disabled_on_links.js", "toolkit/modules/BrowserUtils.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "164a707288b0552bed73064d8d2b80f5c4074b05", "parents": ["918cd8f5c2e9ac67cf2687dfe9842c86a03cf175"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1729255 - [devtools] Store JSON preferences as String instead of Char in PrefsHelper. r=bomsy, a=RyanVM\n\nJSON preferences used to be stored in string preferences, which is compatible with special characters.\nThere should not be any data loss, char prefs seem to gracefully transition to string prefs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D125877", "files": ["devtools/client/shared/prefs.js", "devtools/client/shared/test/browser_prefs-02.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5aeb97e86758b871c3345cfda5c8e0ed75a95669", "parents": ["164a707288b0552bed73064d8d2b80f5c4074b05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@intuitionlibrary.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1734346 - Support backdrops with simple rounded-rect clip cases. r=nical, a=RyanVM\n\nThis allows picture slice backdrops to be supported when they contain\nrounded-rect clip(s) that are in the same coordinate system as the\nprimitive. This is the common case, and allows subpixel AA to be\nused in bookmark menu and other popups that are part of the current\nGecko UI.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D128156", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/subpx-bg-mask-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/subpx-bg-mask.yaml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dbc484a1edb902da4e7fa489e650b3f9a31ffb80", "parents": ["5aeb97e86758b871c3345cfda5c8e0ed75a95669"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1735905 - Upgrade cubeb-pulse to fix a race condition that can lead to shutdown deadlock. r=kinetik, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D128657", "files": [".cargo/config.in", "Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/cubeb-pulse/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/cubeb-pulse/src/backend/stream.rs", "toolkit/library/rust/shared/Cargo.toml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "822169134cdac55a7bb273f74a0bb405b6e6f612", "parents": ["dbc484a1edb902da4e7fa489e650b3f9a31ffb80"], "tags": []}], "date": 1637000436, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "104": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D131482", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9cc492f31cc262d0d40ad4d4d020938d3500a976", "parents": ["822169134cdac55a7bb273f74a0bb405b6e6f612"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740043 - Add fullscreen test; r=smaug a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D131007", "files": ["dom/html/test/browser.ini", "dom/html/test/browser_fullscreen-navigation.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "842ff7e95907af7121d5c86c028bba067c1c274f", "parents": ["9cc492f31cc262d0d40ad4d4d020938d3500a976"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brendan Dahl \u003cbrendan.dahl@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1741445 - Update ESR to pdf.js version 2.11.298. r=calixte, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D131259", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/static/browser_parsable_css.js", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/README.mozilla", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsDefaultPreferences.jsm", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/debugger.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.css", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.yaml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_form.js", "toolkit/modules/AsyncPrefs.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a88ddb41651c9ff9686f4b87d7235ac3e3d58cf6", "parents": ["842ff7e95907af7121d5c86c028bba067c1c274f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1725837 - Adjust detail text size in Downloads Panel, and remove hardcoded width. r=emalysz,flod a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D124243", "files": ["browser/components/downloads/content/downloads.css", "browser/components/downloads/content/downloadsPanel.inc.xhtml", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/downloads.ftl", "browser/locales/l10n-changesets.json", "browser/themes/osx/downloads/downloads.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fdead2dcc9ec809bb6dabad7190b20443b45797b", "parents": ["a88ddb41651c9ff9686f4b87d7235ac3e3d58cf6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1727374 - Implement a JS_HAZ_VALUE_IS_GC_SAFE annotation, saying that *at the time of the annotation*, the given variable does not contain any GC-invalidatable pointers. r=jonco, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123632", "files": ["js/public/GCAnnotations.h", "js/src/devtools/rootAnalysis/analyzeRoots.js", "js/src/devtools/rootAnalysis/run-test.py", "js/src/devtools/rootAnalysis/t/hazards/source.cpp", "js/src/devtools/rootAnalysis/t/hazards/test.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cccf6f79094a0421afff04d73db57f324c47995f", "parents": ["fdead2dcc9ec809bb6dabad7190b20443b45797b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1727374 - Root Init dictionaries to fix rooting hazards. r=peterv, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123633", "files": ["dom/cache/Cache.cpp", "dom/cache/TypeUtils.cpp", "dom/push/PushManager.cpp", "dom/reporting/ReportDeliver.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerOp.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerPrivate.cpp", "dom/worklet/Worklet.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmJS.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c250dd684d8e7e770d562bbb2c7bfac464dc6593", "parents": ["cccf6f79094a0421afff04d73db57f324c47995f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1707642 - Increase message size limit in fuzzing builds. r=nika, a=RyanVM\n\nIf the limit is small, then the fuzzers hit crashes in various places when\npassing in large data structures to DOM APIs, so increase the limit.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D130890", "files": ["ipc/chromium/src/chrome/common/ipc_channel.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9613a40dc2c7440d1d22c7489a00a3c543294162", "parents": ["c250dd684d8e7e770d562bbb2c7bfac464dc6593"], "tags": []}